{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>When arrogance comes</b> — deficient [is] a man, and behold: when a man of arrogance comes, disgrace comes, that smites the children of man." "<b>but with the modest</b> — and with the modest." "<b>wisdom</b> — that they bear the disgrace and do not answer him, and the modest are those who are ashamed to do arrogance, like: 'and walk modestly' (Micah 6:8)."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "Reading חסר איש as 'a man is lacking' (i.e., the word איש is elided from the verse); the syntax of the second clause is compressed and difficult."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:04.185963903Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}